WEBVTT

00:03.790 --> 00:08.080
<i>In the deep, deep forest 
known as the Lost Woods,</i>

00:08.760 --> 00:13.260
<i>a man has taken up residence 
in a deserted, decaying castle.</i>

00:15.650 --> 00:21.700
<i>He is a sorcerer, feared and 
hated by the populace at large...</i>

00:22.730 --> 00:24.210
<i>His name is Zagan.</i>

00:25.940 --> 00:29.900
<i>And right now, he is 
facing a grave challenge.</i>

00:30.450 --> 00:31.710
Master...

00:32.060 --> 00:35.290
is it all right if I ask a question?

00:35.290 --> 00:36.300
What is it?

00:36.970 --> 00:38.010
How exactly...

00:38.580 --> 00:43.730
am I going to be killed?

00:45.010 --> 00:47.230
<i>Hey... hang on a sec!</i>

00:47.230 --> 00:49.150
<i>Why are you assuming I'm going to kill you?!</i>

00:49.400 --> 00:52.650
<i>And what exactly am I supposed to do?!</i>

00:53.270 --> 00:59.280
<i>H-How do you talk to a girl that you like?</i>

02:30.000 --> 02:35.000
<b>Episode 1:
First Love Is Like a Nasty Disease
That Everyone Catches Once</b>

02:35.860 --> 02:38.410
<i>Our story begins the previous morning...</i>

02:41.610 --> 02:42.390
Meyers!

02:42.890 --> 02:44.500
Why are you doing this?!

02:47.380 --> 02:48.570
No!

02:51.900 --> 02:55.850
N-No, you're not Meyers... Who are you?!

02:55.850 --> 02:57.460
What did you do to Meyers?!

03:01.790 --> 03:04.240
That's a pretty tasty face 
you're making there...

03:05.020 --> 03:06.910
And I hate to disappoint you,

03:06.910 --> 03:10.790
but this isn't the kind of 
assault you're hoping for.

03:11.360 --> 03:16.610
See, the face off a living virgin 
makes a hell of a catalyst...

03:16.610 --> 03:17.690
<i>A sorcerer?!</i>

03:18.600 --> 03:21.260
Don't die too easily, now!

03:23.430 --> 03:25.510
No!

03:25.510 --> 03:31.510
Relax! After I've got your face, 
I'll treat your body real nice!

03:32.730 --> 03:34.470
H-Huh?

03:34.470 --> 03:36.110
Wh-Who the hell are you?!

03:36.110 --> 03:38.090
You tell me first.

03:38.090 --> 03:40.570
Do you realize this is someone's 
yard you're shouting in?

03:40.990 --> 03:44.320
I was trying to get some shut-eye, 
but thanks to you, that's not happening.

03:45.330 --> 03:47.790
<i>Shit, this must be his territory.</i>

03:48.160 --> 03:49.290
H-Hang on!

03:49.290 --> 03:51.330
We're both sorcerers!

03:51.330 --> 03:54.760
Let me go and I'll share the 
fruits of my research with you!

03:54.760 --> 03:59.880
I don't need any sorcery that
 requires flaying people.

04:11.880 --> 04:13.350
<i>I overdid it.</i>

04:13.680 --> 04:16.480
<i>She's absolutely gonna be 
traumatized when she wakes up.</i>

04:16.800 --> 04:19.730
<i>G-Gotta keep my cool. I'm a sorcerer.</i>

04:20.310 --> 04:22.380
<i>This'll be easy to fix.</i>

04:22.380 --> 04:23.740
Rewound Cycle.

04:39.580 --> 04:43.190
All that really does is put 
everything back where it was...

04:43.910 --> 04:45.340
But since the blood is gone,

04:45.620 --> 04:47.350
she'll probably think it was a dream.

04:52.150 --> 04:53.770
A cross?

04:54.080 --> 04:55.770
Is she with the Church?

04:56.150 --> 04:59.770
<i>The self-proclaimed apostles of 
God. Enemies of all sorcerers.</i>

05:00.220 --> 05:02.440
<i>I actually saved her,</i>

05:02.440 --> 05:05.280
<i>but I'm likely to get
 blamed for the attack.</i>

05:05.280 --> 05:07.950
<i>Not that I really care.</i>

05:11.790 --> 05:14.750
<i>If I drop her on the road to a town, 
someone's bound to find her.</i>

05:19.120 --> 05:21.170
<i>Something's interfering with 
my translocation sorcery?</i>

05:21.540 --> 05:25.060
<i>This is my territory.
 I've got protective fields all around.</i>

05:25.060 --> 05:27.500
<i>This isn't a trick that just 
any sorcerer could pull.</i>

05:34.120 --> 05:38.160
I'd appreciate if you wouldn't muck around 
with my casting circles, Barbatos.

05:38.780 --> 05:43.330
Hey, Zagan. You look like shit, as usual.

05:43.900 --> 05:45.650
And so do you.

05:46.000 --> 05:48.800
So, what? Did I interrupt some kind of party?

05:48.800 --> 05:52.330
Just teaching a lesson to a creep who 
was making a fuss in my yard, that's all.

05:52.610 --> 05:55.770
A creep? Where do you get off, man?

05:55.770 --> 05:59.040
We're sorcerers. The only thing we 
respect is our own pursuit of power.

05:59.390 --> 06:01.920
Other people's lives and 
livelihoods are nothing but

06:01.920 --> 06:03.720
fuel for that, which we take, 
if we feel like it.

06:03.720 --> 06:07.010
That's what it means to 
be a sorcerer, right?

06:08.010 --> 06:12.660
Hey... this girl's got a 
decent amount of mana.

06:12.660 --> 06:14.180
You gonna sacrifice her or something?

06:14.650 --> 06:17.390
Sacrificial sorcery isn't my style.

06:24.720 --> 06:28.150
What a waste. You should've let me have 
her if you weren't going to use her!

06:29.420 --> 06:33.280
I'm going to bed. I was up 
late reading sorcerous tomes.

06:33.560 --> 06:35.450
If you need something, come back later.

06:35.690 --> 06:39.920
Come on, man. Don't be like 
that after I came all this way!

06:40.400 --> 06:45.170
You could always just tweak your 
brain with adrenaline to wake up.

06:45.170 --> 06:48.880
That sort of thing is how you ended up
 looking like such a mess yourself.

06:48.880 --> 06:52.000
Manipulating the body is 
fundamental for sorcery!

06:52.000 --> 06:54.640
It keeps us healthy and long-lived.

06:54.940 --> 06:57.640
Even if it's got a limit of
 about a thousand years.

06:59.280 --> 07:02.230
I've got some real interesting news, Zagan.

07:03.190 --> 07:07.610
Did you know one of the 
Archdemons, Marchosias, is dead?

07:11.040 --> 07:12.240
<i>The Archdemons.</i>

07:12.240 --> 07:15.600
<i>Earning that title gets you an
 incredible amount of mana,</i>

07:15.600 --> 07:19.230
<i>along with the authority to 
command lower-ranked sorcerers.</i>

07:19.230 --> 07:20.910
<i>They are the pinnacle of sorcery.</i>

07:21.470 --> 07:23.890
<i>Of the 13 Archdemons,</i>

07:23.890 --> 07:29.180
<i>the longest lived—who had been around for 
a millennium—passed away the other day.</i>

07:30.350 --> 07:33.960
See, now you're all curious, huh?

07:33.960 --> 07:37.260
But I thought you were 
going to bed! What a shame!

07:37.260 --> 07:40.350
If you're going to talk, then talk!

07:40.350 --> 07:41.350
All right, all right.

07:42.440 --> 07:47.070
There's apparently gonna be a huge auction 
at Marchosias' territory, Kianoides.

07:47.390 --> 07:50.620
From legitimate merchandise to the kind of 
thing you and I would be interested in.

07:50.620 --> 07:51.530
Are you saying...

07:51.530 --> 07:53.490
I am!

07:53.790 --> 07:57.740
An Archdemon's legacy is 
gonna be up for auction!

08:04.560 --> 08:07.500
And I thought you actually had news for me.

08:07.800 --> 08:11.510
But you just want to borrow money 
for the auction, don't you?

08:11.850 --> 08:14.590
I could just buy the legacy 
for myself, y'know?

08:14.590 --> 08:16.470
Come on, man, no fair!

08:16.470 --> 08:18.420
I was the one who told you about it!

08:18.420 --> 08:20.140
Well, you can ask someone else.

08:20.140 --> 08:24.200
You're the only sorcerer 
I know who'd loan me any money!

08:24.950 --> 08:29.330
Come on, I'll help you pick out 
some nice chicks in exchange!

08:29.330 --> 08:30.900
Women, huh...

08:31.580 --> 08:36.320
<i>I'm kind of interested, but they seem 
like more trouble than they'd be worth...</i>

08:40.870 --> 08:42.820
The guards seem weirdly on edge.

08:42.820 --> 08:45.790
Yeah, that'd be due to 
the serial kidnappings.

08:46.110 --> 08:52.200
Some dumbasses have been snatching up 
young women for sorcerous experiments.

08:52.200 --> 08:55.160
Sounds like a risky proposition.

08:55.160 --> 08:57.340
They're basically picking 
a fight with the Church.

08:57.570 --> 08:59.190
And for what?

08:59.190 --> 09:00.470
Couldn't tell you.

09:00.720 --> 09:03.780
<i>Maybe they're planning on 
summoning something significant?</i>

09:03.780 --> 09:05.350
<i>Like an actual demon.</i>

09:05.800 --> 09:08.930
<i>Then again, that's like 
something out of a fairy tale.</i>

09:11.400 --> 09:13.650
Come to think of it, Zagan...

09:13.650 --> 09:17.060
Aren't you suspected of being 
behind these kidnappings?

09:17.060 --> 09:18.510
That's stupid.

09:18.510 --> 09:23.590
How practical can sacrificial sorcery 
really be, when you get down to it?

09:24.450 --> 09:25.930
True enough.

09:25.930 --> 09:29.830
And it's not like you have enough 
friends to help you out, either!

09:30.890 --> 09:33.800
<i>I never really thought friends 
were a necessity, anyway.</i>

09:55.040 --> 09:56.380
Check it out, Zagan.

09:57.400 --> 09:59.290
We've got a regular bunch of celebrities.

10:00.400 --> 10:02.490
Kimaris the Black Blade.

10:00.570 --> 10:02.490
<b>Kimaris the Black Blade</b>

10:02.820 --> 10:04.320
Gremory the Enchantress..

10:03.040 --> 10:05.000
<b>Gremory the Enchantress</b>

10:04.320 --> 10:08.000
And there's even Valefor the Apparition.

10:05.500 --> 10:08.000
<b>Valefor the Apparition</b>

10:08.350 --> 10:13.500
<i>Second names... are something 
like titles for sorcerers.</i>

10:14.150 --> 10:15.130
Are they strong?

10:15.360 --> 10:16.620
Oh, yeah.

10:16.620 --> 10:21.050
They're candidates to become the 13th 
Archdemon now that old Marchosias is gone.

10:21.050 --> 10:23.060
Granted, so am I.

10:23.060 --> 10:25.040
The next Archdemon...

10:25.040 --> 10:26.180
Who makes that call?

10:26.880 --> 10:30.150
The surviving 12 apparently debate it.

10:30.150 --> 10:33.280
Kimaris, look over there.

10:34.070 --> 10:37.650
The sickly-looking guy who's loafing around...

10:37.650 --> 10:39.000
What was his name again?

10:39.000 --> 10:42.150
I believe that is Barbatos the Purgatory.

10:42.880 --> 10:46.240
And that sour-looking one 
next to him is called Zagan.

10:46.540 --> 10:48.790
He's young, and without a title,

10:48.790 --> 10:52.860
but for some reason his name came up
 among the Archdemon candidates.

10:53.580 --> 10:55.550
Ladies and gentlemen,

10:55.550 --> 11:00.620
who have finally come to our final, 
and most remarkable lot for the auction!

11:06.690 --> 11:09.530
This merchandise was previously scheduled

11:09.530 --> 11:13.500
to come into the possession of 
Archdemon Marchosias himself.

11:13.500 --> 11:19.370
However, with Lord Marchosias' 
passing, that deal fell through,

11:19.370 --> 11:22.340
and it now is on us to see 
that it finds a new owner!

11:22.340 --> 11:24.460
Wait, what about all his stuff?

11:24.460 --> 11:28.720
This is probably a catalyst 
that he had picked out.

11:30.260 --> 11:35.010
A member of the legendary race 
from the distant Norden holy land...

11:35.010 --> 11:36.550
An elf!

11:46.010 --> 11:51.020
<b>An Archdemon's Dilemma:
How to Love Your Elf Bride</b>

11:51.480 --> 11:57.770
As you're all aware, elves are closer 
to gods and nature spirits than humans!

11:58.180 --> 12:01.330
And as you can see with this one, 
she has striking white hair!

12:01.330 --> 12:06.530
This isn't dyed, folks. You're looking at an 
extremely rare, naturally platinum-locked elf!

12:06.910 --> 12:09.080
Her magical properties
 make her extremely valuable,

12:09.480 --> 12:12.660
to say nothing of her worth as a love slave!

12:12.960 --> 12:16.670
And if you can afford the price,
 she's yours for doing with as you please!

12:17.230 --> 12:20.590
Let's start the bidding at ten thousand—

12:19.380 --> 12:20.590
One million!

12:24.090 --> 12:26.430
Uh, Zagan...

12:26.660 --> 12:28.970
One million gold Kuriotes.

12:30.300 --> 12:32.060
Thank you very much, sir!

12:32.060 --> 12:34.100
What an amazing bid!

12:34.100 --> 12:36.600
Do we have any others?

12:34.100 --> 12:37.770
Damn, Zagan! I know she's 
an elf, but that's so much!

12:38.000 --> 12:40.650
<i>What is this feeling in my chest?</i>

12:41.030 --> 12:42.480
<i>She's so lovely.</i>

12:42.480 --> 12:44.800
<i>Is that the right way to express it?</i>

12:45.210 --> 12:48.470
<i>I want to help her,
I want to see her smiling...</i>

12:49.920 --> 12:52.540
<i>And I want to touch her.</i>

12:54.660 --> 12:58.670
It's like I've finally found something 
I didn't know I was looking for.

12:58.980 --> 13:02.460
What the hell kinda sorcery 
are you going to use her for?

13:11.170 --> 13:12.640
Congratulations, sir!

13:12.940 --> 13:17.090
The sorcerer Zagan has purchased 
one white-haired elf!

13:22.800 --> 13:25.900
<i>What now? What do I say to her?</i>

13:26.440 --> 13:30.800
<i>Is she okay? She's not under 
some sorcery right now, is she?</i>

13:30.800 --> 13:33.320
Any problems, Mr. Zagan?

13:33.320 --> 13:34.270
Uh, no!

13:36.690 --> 13:37.910
What's this?

13:37.910 --> 13:39.880
The collar must keep her mana contained.

13:40.240 --> 13:44.550
She's likely to run off without it,
 so please, be careful.

13:44.880 --> 13:48.930
That said, none of us know 
how to remove it, anyway.

13:49.920 --> 13:52.140
Is she conscious?

13:52.140 --> 13:53.970
Not to worry!

13:54.330 --> 13:58.150
She's been preserved in 
her natural state, sir!

13:58.150 --> 14:02.120
To be honest, she's got 
such incredible capacity,

14:02.120 --> 14:05.600
ordinary sorcery hasn't proven effective.

14:05.600 --> 14:06.930
I believe you.

14:07.580 --> 14:10.120
<i>First, I'd like to talk with her.</i>

14:10.740 --> 14:15.750
I can't wait to hear the 
sweet sounds she makes!

14:21.640 --> 14:22.260
<i>Huh?</i>

14:22.650 --> 14:25.530
<i>Did that come out weird?</i>

14:25.530 --> 14:31.580
<i>This is what happens when someone who thought
women were too much trouble just moments ago</i>

14:31.580 --> 14:34.620
<i>falls in love for the first time in his life.</i>

14:42.950 --> 14:45.280
Well, I've brought her home, but...

14:47.750 --> 14:50.950
<i>I should've asked Barbatos about this.</i>

14:50.950 --> 14:53.380
<i>What am I supposed to say to her?</i>

14:53.380 --> 14:58.710
<i>But I have to say something eventually.</i>

14:59.370 --> 15:01.080
"The sky is beautiful today."

15:02.470 --> 15:05.340
<i>No, come on. Even I can do better than that.</i>

15:05.740 --> 15:08.840
<i>Besides, we can't see the sky in here,
 and the weather is awful!</i>

15:09.360 --> 15:11.470
"What do you think of the castle?"

15:13.910 --> 15:16.220
<i>Get a grip, man!</i>

15:16.500 --> 15:21.200
<i>"It's like execution grounds, or maybe hell"
 is all I can think she'd say!</i>

15:21.200 --> 15:22.100
<i>Not to mention...</i>

15:22.640 --> 15:25.660
<i>Why didn't I clean up 
before bringing her home?!</i>

15:26.330 --> 15:27.560
Master...

15:28.460 --> 15:30.900
Is it all right if I ask a question?

15:31.200 --> 15:32.750
<i>She talked!</i>

15:32.750 --> 15:36.410
<i>She's got a sweet voice 
like the ringing of a bell.</i>

15:36.850 --> 15:38.230
What is it?

15:38.230 --> 15:40.060
<i>Why'd I say it like that?!</i>

15:40.060 --> 15:42.670
<i>I sounded completely annoyed just now!</i>

15:43.360 --> 15:44.450
How exactly...

15:44.990 --> 15:50.470
am I going to be killed?

15:57.040 --> 16:01.900
If I know beforehand, I believe 
I'll be able to better prepare myself...

16:02.350 --> 16:04.100
Wait, wait, wait!

16:04.100 --> 16:05.770
I'm not going to kill you!

16:05.770 --> 16:08.360
If anything, I need you alive!

16:08.800 --> 16:09.950
Then...

16:09.950 --> 16:14.860
I should be expecting something 
worse than death, with no release?

16:15.950 --> 16:17.370
<i>You've got it wrong!</i>

16:17.370 --> 16:19.870
<i>All this stuff belonged to 
the castle's previous owner!</i>

16:19.870 --> 16:23.620
<i>I just never got rid of it because 
it seemed like a lot of work!</i>

16:28.080 --> 16:29.780
My name is Zagan.

16:29.780 --> 16:33.340
As you can tell, I'm a sorcerer, 
but I have no interest in torture.

16:33.880 --> 16:35.200
Now, then...

16:39.090 --> 16:40.530
So...

16:40.530 --> 16:41.600
<i>This is ridiculous!</i>

16:41.600 --> 16:46.050
<i>Why am I having so much trouble 
just asking for her name?!</i>

16:48.040 --> 16:49.620
I apologize.

16:50.660 --> 16:52.900
My name is Nephelia.

16:53.260 --> 16:54.460
Nephelia...

16:55.380 --> 16:56.870
<i>What a beautiful name.</i>

16:57.250 --> 17:00.860
Nephelia... what, exactly? 
What is your family name?

17:00.860 --> 17:02.120
I have none.

17:02.500 --> 17:05.500
If you find it distasteful, 
please, just call me Nephy.

17:06.120 --> 17:07.350
Can I?!

17:07.350 --> 17:08.080
Yes...

17:08.370 --> 17:12.760
<i>Not only is her name beautiful, 
she's got a cute nickname like Nephy!</i>

17:13.170 --> 17:18.880
Is it common for elves 
not to have a family name?

17:18.880 --> 17:19.550
No...

17:19.950 --> 17:22.560
I just happen to be a cursed child.

17:24.170 --> 17:25.310
A cursed child?

17:25.610 --> 17:29.640
Excuse me... but, why are you asking?

17:29.640 --> 17:30.320
Well...

17:32.420 --> 17:33.570
You don't need to worry.

17:35.680 --> 17:36.950
I'm a virgin.

17:37.910 --> 17:39.410
Y-You...

17:39.410 --> 17:42.340
Do you realize what you're talking about?!

17:43.360 --> 17:48.340
I thought you were concerned about my 
value as a subject for your experiments.

17:48.340 --> 17:49.800
Don't misunderstand me!

17:49.800 --> 17:51.840
I have no intention of experimenting on you.

17:52.130 --> 17:54.960
Why did you buy me, then?

17:58.220 --> 18:00.540
You don't need to know that.

18:01.090 --> 18:03.520
<i>What am I even saying?!</i>

18:03.800 --> 18:06.200
<i>But "I fell head over heels for 
you at an underground auction"</i>

18:06.200 --> 18:08.280
<i>"and spent my entire fortune buying you"</i>

18:08.280 --> 18:10.360
<i>obviously makes me sound 
like some kind of pervert.</i>

18:10.750 --> 18:12.720
<i>And if we're going to be living 
together in the future,</i>

18:12.720 --> 18:15.280
<i>I couldn't bear her looking 
at me like that...</i>

18:16.080 --> 18:17.610
<i>Living together?!</i>

18:18.160 --> 18:21.250
<i>I'm going to be under the same 
roof as this adorable girl?!</i>

18:21.840 --> 18:23.950
<i>I need to calm down. I'm a sorcerer.</i>

18:24.240 --> 18:27.150
<i>A powerful sorcerer should 
always maintain his composure.</i>

18:30.320 --> 18:33.840
Nephy, for now, I'm going 
to provide you with a room.

18:34.220 --> 18:35.840
Pick out whichever you would like.

18:36.150 --> 18:39.340
Are you asking me to choose where I'll die?

18:39.640 --> 18:41.850
I told you, I'm not going to kill you!

18:41.850 --> 18:45.760
I just don't understand why you wouldn't...

18:46.460 --> 18:48.600
Are you saying that I'm 
not going to be killed,

18:48.950 --> 18:51.860
no matter what purpose you have for me?

18:51.860 --> 18:53.110
<i>I get it.</i>

18:53.830 --> 18:55.570
<i>Of course...</i>

18:55.570 --> 18:58.180
<i>She was caught and sold off as a slave.</i>

18:58.180 --> 19:03.120
<i>She was probably told that she was going to be 
a test subject or a sacrifice this entire time.</i>

19:04.280 --> 19:06.620
<i>I don't know what this 
"cursed child" business is,</i>

19:06.900 --> 19:08.750
<i>and she doesn't seem to 
want to talk about it,</i>

19:09.250 --> 19:11.150
<i>so she probably doesn't 
have a home to return to.</i>

19:11.840 --> 19:13.130
<i>It was the same for me.</i>

19:14.210 --> 19:15.630
<i>Not only did I not have a family name,</i>

19:16.120 --> 19:17.770
<i>I don't even remember my parents.</i>

19:18.480 --> 19:20.890
<i>The first thing I do remember 
is living in the trash...</i>

19:23.200 --> 19:27.310
<i>And being called by the name Zagan.</i>

19:31.150 --> 19:33.730
I bought you because I need you.

19:34.080 --> 19:36.110
So, no more of this dying talk.

19:36.450 --> 19:38.610
Need... me?

19:38.610 --> 19:40.450
You mean that?

19:40.760 --> 19:43.820
Yes. So for now, you'll live for my sake.

19:50.160 --> 19:50.990
Yes.

19:58.010 --> 20:00.590
Now, about your room...

20:01.190 --> 20:02.720
<i>What would be good?</i>

20:02.720 --> 20:04.460
<i>Maybe someplace with a view...</i>

20:05.310 --> 20:06.880
Do you mind heights?

20:06.880 --> 20:07.680
No.

20:08.090 --> 20:11.380
Feel free to hang me by the 
neck or the wrists as you like.

20:11.380 --> 20:13.690
I'm not talking about torture!

20:14.010 --> 20:15.600
Forgive me.

20:15.600 --> 20:19.050
I couldn't think of anything else
 when you mentioned heights.

20:19.050 --> 20:21.690
Please, scrounge up a little more hope.

20:33.300 --> 20:36.550
Be careful. Watch where you're walking.

20:36.550 --> 20:37.870
R-Right.

20:41.970 --> 20:47.000
<i>Huh... Am I holding hands 
with Nephy right now?</i>

20:47.000 --> 20:48.940
<i>But it'd be weird to let go.</i>

20:49.900 --> 20:52.950
<i>They're so soft, and warm...</i>

20:55.980 --> 20:57.400
This room isn't usually in use.

20:58.310 --> 21:00.280
It might not be very tidy, but...

21:07.060 --> 21:09.810
You may take my head as 
it pleases you, Master.

21:09.810 --> 21:11.290
Seriously, stop!

21:11.550 --> 21:13.540
This is, you know...

21:13.540 --> 21:17.580
A trap to protect the castle 
from airborne enemies!

21:18.220 --> 21:20.420
<i>Even I have trouble buying that.</i>

21:20.720 --> 21:24.030
However, I can see how it'd be in the way.

21:24.480 --> 21:25.850
Let me dispose of it.

21:37.150 --> 21:40.020
<i>I have my doubts about it's 
function as a room, but...</i>

21:40.300 --> 21:43.700
<i>At least she's got nothing 
to be afraid of.</i>

21:44.970 --> 21:48.150
I've never seen such 
destructive sorcery before.

21:48.150 --> 21:51.620
<i>Okay, so maybe blasting away with attack 
sorcery out of the blue is intimidating!</i>

21:51.620 --> 21:55.750
<i>This is what happens when the only 
person I ever talk to is Barbatos!</i>

21:56.000 --> 21:59.140
This won't do after all. It's too dreary.

21:59.140 --> 22:02.030
Is that really the word for it?

22:16.730 --> 22:18.340
You like the moon?

22:20.540 --> 22:21.820
I don't know.

22:29.520 --> 22:31.040
I don't think we can reach it.

22:31.040 --> 22:32.570
That makes sense.

22:38.610 --> 22:40.110
U-Um...

22:41.400 --> 22:44.370
Is it all right if I stay in this room?

22:47.590 --> 22:49.760
You don't mind all of... this, then?

22:49.760 --> 22:50.610
No.

22:52.190 --> 22:55.350
Because it's the room you 
prepared for me, Master.

22:56.450 --> 22:59.760
F-Fine, then. Use it how you see fit.

22:59.760 --> 23:01.350
Thank you.

23:04.320 --> 23:06.280
Is something wrong?

23:06.280 --> 23:07.070
No...

23:08.000 --> 23:12.280
It's just been a long time since 
anyone thanked me for anything.

23:13.460 --> 23:17.040
I think it's been a long time 
since I've given thanks, too.

23:17.620 --> 23:18.960
I see.

23:18.960 --> 23:19.760
Yes...

23:21.170 --> 23:25.580
<i>It was on this night that 
their long cohabitation...</i>

23:25.580 --> 23:29.280
<i>and their very, very long story began.</i>

23:30.010 --> 23:35.010
<b>Next Time:
First Love With Social Anxiety Tastes a Lot Like Moldy Bread</b>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
<b>Crap, what
do I do?</b>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
<b>What do
I do?</b>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
<b>She's so cute
it's painful...!!!
Am I gonna be able
to sleep tonight?!</b>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
<b>Zagan's internal
monologue</b>
